    "body": "Fixes #39878\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\n`vim.fs.dir()` and `vim.fs.find()` currently drops filesystem errors from `uv.fs_scandir()`. If a directory cannot be read, callers see the same result as an empty directory.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nThis change adds optional error reporting to `vim.fs.dir()` and `vim.fs.find()` while preserving existing behavior for callers that do not handle errors.\r\n\r\nFor `dir()`:\r\n* Root directory scan failures are returned as a secondary return value\r\n* Recursive scan failures are surfaced through the iterator as a third return value (`err`).\r\n* If a directory is unreadable, but does not need to be scanned (since its at a greater depth than the specified `depth`) then an error is not returned.\r\n\r\nFor `find()`:\r\n* Traversal errors are returned as a list/array of `{ path, err }` as a secondary return value.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal it, err = vim.fs.dir(path, { depth = math.huge })\r\n\r\nif err then\r\n  -- Root directory could not be scanned.\r\nend\r\n\r\nfor name, type, err in it do\r\n  if err then\r\n    -- Directory could not be traversed.\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n```\r\n```lua\r\nlocal matches, errors = vim.fs.find('abc')\r\n-- errors = {\r\n--   { path = 'abc/foo/bar', err = 'EACCES: permission denied: foo/bar' },\r\n--   { path = 'abc/foo/baz', err = 'EACCES: permission denied: foo/baz' },\r\n-- }\r\n```\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-01T11:18:08Z",
