            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "this example shows that `fs.dir()` is now much more clumsy to use. \n\ni will push an update that changes it to:\n\n```lua\nfor name, type, err in vim.fs.dir(path) do\n  if err then\n    -- Failed to scan a child directory (or root directory).\n  end\nend\n```\n\nplease think about this kind of thing in future PRs, don't just do whatever the AI suggests.\n",
            "commit_id": "1035a9fb5df1ed7c5cab99fa4c0686c2c9ef0e37",
            "created_at": "2026-07-01T09:12:00Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -2596,6 +2596,20 @@ vim.fs.dir({path}, {opts})                                      *vim.fs.dir()*\n     Gets an iterator over items found in `path` (normalized via\n     |vim.fs.normalize()|).\n \n+    Example: >lua\n+        local it, err = vim.fs.dir(path)\n+\n+        if err then\n+          -- Failed to scan the root directory\n+        end\n+\n+        for name, type, err in it do\n+          if err then\n+            -- Failed to scan a child directory\n+          end\n+        end",
